      "id": "claim_a6ca8ab2a307452e8c8254620cc6d5ee",
      "statement": "`fetch(url, timeout=30, max_retries=3)` accepts only non-empty HTTP(S) URL strings and retrieves them through a fresh `primp` client configured to impersonate Safari on macOS with HTTP/2-only requests; `render(url, wait_time=2)` additionally accepts `file://` URLs and is a separate browser-rendering path.",
